Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["DisplacementReduce", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"fcc42c80-73e0-4f7c-89d8-43467efe65a7"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["DisplacementReduce"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementReduce", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "85a82488-0c4e-4268-887b-70bf2c1d4f45"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "contracts each value of the displacement ",
 StyleBox["d", "TI"],
 " to its metric centre, the vertices of least eccentricity within the value, \
repeated until nothing changes.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"85d1b8fc-0cfe-4546-8097-b430c5bb156e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: for a set ",
 StyleBox["S", "TI"],
 " of vertices let ",
 StyleBox["c(S) = { x \[Element] S : max_{y \[Element] S} d(x, y) is least }",
   "TI"],
 ". The reduced value at ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is the fixed point of ",
 StyleBox["S \[RightTeeArrow] c(S)", "TI"],
 " starting from ",
 StyleBox["D(v)", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"32259118-416a-4b6b-8a19-26e605fb81ba"],

Cell["\<\
Each reduced value is a subset of the original one, so no step becomes \
longer. A single vertex stays. A set whose vertices are all equally central, \
such as any two vertices or all the vertices of a cycle, stays as it is: a \
tie the metric does not break.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"92d65249-e7e1-4414-ae3f-aabfd6457f25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The values of a displacement are sets because the metric does not always \
decide: half a step, the midpoints of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DisplacementSum"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementSum", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "29f440c3-1f38-48f4-90db-6d6d3b92e731"],
 ", the continuations of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["DisplacementScale"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/DisplacementScale", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "acd332da-820e-47be-a972-03c4a5abf75e"],
 " on the hexagonal tiling. The reduction keeps the part the metric decides."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c9a2b0d4-e061-4d28-bfb5-0fe008aac468"]
}, Open  ]],

